    Bug 1933970 - Fix alignment problems for toolbar button menus. r=Paenglab,micah


    Nested WebExtension entries (inside of a WebExtension `menupopup`)
    need a gutter, if they do not have an icon, or can be selected/toggled.
    Otherwise these menus can look ragged, as shown by the screenshots
    attached to the phab.

    This is usually controlled by the `needsgutter` attribute, but setting
    it here does not help, because it gets removed by a global listener for
    the `popupshowing` event in [1].

    This patch is adding a `webextension-menupopup` class (similar to our
    `webextension-group-separator` class in [2]), and adds the required
    changes to the CSS files.

    The bugzilla bug itself has a reproducer add-on, to verify the actual
    issue in an unpatched Thunderbird, and the fixed alignment after
    applying the patch.

    [1]: https://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/rev/495dafe9d89894e4768afe6d978139351574cc84/toolkit/content/widgets/menupopup.js#29
    [2]: https://searchfox.org/comm-central/rev/61d8d2a48e1cbdab1ba3c43af6bb679cc18de831/mail/components/extensions/parent/ext-menus.js#115

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D232700

